## Computer Vision Best Practices

### Image Processing
- Always validate image dimensions and channels
- Use appropriate color space conversions (BGR ↔ RGB ↔ HSV)
- Apply noise filtering before detection (Gaussian blur, median filter)
- Implement multi-scale processing for robust detection

### Detection & Tracking
- Use confidence thresholds to filter low-quality detections
- Implement multi-frame consistency checks
- Apply non-maximum suppression for overlapping detections
- Use Kalman filters or similar for smooth tracking

### Performance Optimization
- Resize images for processing speed when possible
- Use vectorized operations with numpy
- Implement frame skipping for real-time processing
- Cache expensive computations

